From: Tejas Vijay Kanfade <tkanfade@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:16:07 +0530
Subject: build: pass PAL_CONFIG_DIR to compiler and use in SNDPARSER

PR #92 adds --with-pal-config-dir configure option but does not pass
PAL_CONFIG_DIR to the compiler via AM_CPPFLAGS. Without this flag,
ResourceManager.cpp falls back to the hardcoded SNDPARSER path
"/etc/card-defs.xml" regardless of the configure option value.

Also pass PAL_PLUGIN_DIR and PAL_DATA_DIR for consistency with the
other directory macros used in the source.

Update SNDPARSER in ResourceManager.cpp to use PAL_CONFIG_DIR so
that the card-defs.xml path is controlled by the configure option.
The default value of PAL_CONFIG_DIR is "/etc" which preserves the
existing upstream behaviour.

This is a gap in PR #92 discovered during QLI validation on iq-9075-evk:
without this fix PAL fails to find card-defs.xml when audioreach-conf
moves it to /etc/audioreach/ via --with-pal-config-dir=/etc/audioreach.

Validated on iq-9075-evk with QLI build.

Origin: https://github.com/AudioReach/audioreach-pal/pull/96

Signed-off-by: Tejas Vijay Kanfade <tkanfade@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 Makefile.am                              | 1 +
 resource_manager/src/ResourceManager.cpp | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 8cda917..171203f 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@ AM_CPPFLAGS += -D__unused=__attribute__\(\(__unused__\)\) -DLINUX_ENABLED
 AM_CPPFLAGS += -DCONFIG_GSL
 AM_CPPFLAGS += -DPAL_PLUGIN_DIR=\"@PAL_PLUGIN_DIR@\"
 AM_CPPFLAGS += -DPAL_DATA_DIR=\"@PAL_DATA_DIR@\"
+AM_CPPFLAGS += -DPAL_CONFIG_DIR=\"@PAL_CONFIG_DIR@\"
 
 library_includedir = $(includedir)/audioreach-pal
 lib_LTLIBRARIES     = libaudioreach-pal.la
diff --git a/resource_manager/src/ResourceManager.cpp b/resource_manager/src/ResourceManager.cpp
index 1b09664..d715f56 100644
--- a/resource_manager/src/ResourceManager.cpp
+++ b/resource_manager/src/ResourceManager.cpp
@@ -81,8 +81,11 @@
 #define VBAT_BCL_SUFFIX "-vbat"
 #define SPKR_PROT_SUFFIX "-prot"
 
+#ifndef PAL_CONFIG_DIR
+#define PAL_CONFIG_DIR "/etc"
+#endif
 #if defined(FEATURE_IPQ_OPENWRT) || defined(LINUX_ENABLED)
-#define SNDPARSER "/etc/card-defs.xml"
+#define SNDPARSER PAL_CONFIG_DIR "/card-defs.xml"
 #define SNDPARSER_NATIVE "/etc/card-defs-native.xml"
 #else
 #define SNDPARSER "/vendor/etc/card-defs.xml"
